{
 "scope": "Codimension-m coarea program, step 1: the linear area formula in the repository normalization, and the identification of affine fibres with Lebesgue measure. NO coarea formula and NO C1 area formula proved; no hole migrated. The log-concave Cheeger-Buser line belongs to collaborator Wang Haocheng and was not touched.",
 "head": "34b92695ece4f636a1a7f1eafbbf41c685ee0348",
 "origin_main": "34b92695ece4f636a1a7f1eafbbf41c685ee0348",
 "incoming_receipt": "build/verification/20260916T122340.295044Z/report.json",
 "incoming_snapshot": "c0e5cd2924db9e48eb1746067c434f410556f4907d36622c3c8664b4ac86c570",
 "incoming_entries": 510,
 "incoming_status": "passed",
 "new_lemmas": [
  "KLS.hausdorffNormalized_image_linearMap",
  "KLS.adjoint_apply_linearIsometry",
  "KLS.normDet_linearIsometry",
  "KLS.hausdorffNormalized_image_linearIsometry",
  "KLS.hausdorffNormalized_image_affine",
  "KLS.hausdorffNormalized_fiber"
 ],
 "why_needed": "Mathlib proves the linear area formula for the raw Hausdorff measure, while every measure in this repository is the classical omega_d (diam/2)^d normalization. The two differ by a dimensional constant, and the inner integral of the codimension-m coarea formula must come out with no residual constant.",
 "key_results": {
  "exact_volume_factor": "both sides of the normalized formula carry the same constant, so it cancels and normDet is exact",
  "isometry_factor": "a linear isometric embedding has normDet = 1",
  "fibre_statement": "a translated isometric slice carries exactly Lebesgue measure on its parameter space; specialized to ker L this is the fibre of a linear map",
  "codimension_count": "for surjective L, finrank (ker L) = finrank V - finrank W, audited separately"
 },
 "reused_not_reproved": [
  "FunctionalInequalities.Analysis.hausdorffNormalized_image_add_left",
  "FunctionalInequalities.KLS.hausdorffNormalized_finrank_eq_volume",
  "LinearMap.hausdorffMeasure_image (Mathlib)",
  "LinearMap.normDet_sq (Mathlib)"
 ],
